      "file": "docs/adr/0207-a-worker-runs-behind-an-executor-seam-and-the.md",
      "line": "56-64",
      "area": "context",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "tag": "nit",
      "description": "The ADR says the host replays a `pup_signal` line \"through the same function the local command calls\" and that \"a signal that function refuses is told to the worker.\" For a question, `markSessionQuestion` (`src/core/session-lifecycle.service.ts` L754-760) refuses nothing: it only calls `appendEvent` with an already-built payload. The refusal lives in `askedQuestion` (L767), which throws `QuestionRefusedError` for empty text, too many options or a bad `--recommend`. An implementer following the ADR literally would replay a remote `ask` without validating it, and the sandbox shim cannot validate on the host's behalf. The ADR should name `askedQuestion` as part of the replay path for `ask`.",
